{
  "summary": "The experiment tested an RNA-only model using PCA encoding without image or multimodal components, establishing a baseline for RNA-only performance. Validation accuracy of 0.485 and F1 of 0.464 suggest moderate baseline performance, though uncertainty remains about whether multimodal approaches could achieve higher scores. The absence of comparative evidence limits conclusions about the efficacy of RNA-only versus multimodal designs."
}

